WEBVTT

00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:14,720
I'm thinking of buying some small fruit trees to get clean fruit in a few years.

00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:21,120
How important is it to buy trees that are organic trees, like organic apple trees,

00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:27,280
from the start versus conventional trees that you might get at the hardware store or something?

00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:33,280
If we buy conventional will this synthetics be out in a few years by the time the tree

00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:39,600
matures and we get fruit? Or if we buy conventional will the young trees struggle without the

00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:48,000
synthetics they were started on? So, we planted, you know, we do a lot of gardening,

00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,080
I think that's why this question was asked. We planted different fruit trees and you can buy

00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:02,080
organic apple trees. I don't know about any of the other fruit trees, but I have seen the

00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:09,040
organic apple trees. Now, in truth, is it important to buy an organic tree?

00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:16,960
My answer to that is, I don't think so. I don't think it's important to buy an organic tree.

00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:21,600
Now, what's the difference between an organic tree and an non-organic tree? Well,

00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:30,240
the non-organic conventionally grown tree probably had been sprayed at some point in time,

00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:36,400
but in truth, if you're buying a tree, that is, you know, the diameter of the tree is an

00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:41,920
inch to an inch and a half thick, which is typically a lot of fruit trees. The chance that they sprayed

00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:49,040
it with something is zero. They're not trying to get fruit. Therefore, you know, they're not

00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:54,240
spraying these trees. So, I don't think there's an issue with that. Even if they did spray,

00:01:54,960 --> 00:02:02,640
the trees for apples for the worms to keep, you know, they would be picking the fruit off of it any

00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:07,680
how they don't want the trees to be fruity. So, I don't even think they would spend the money to

00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:15,680
buy the spray to spray the trees. So, I do not think it's important to spend, you know, three times

00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:21,440
the price to get an organic apple tree. If you're going to grow it organically, like our apple trees,

00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:27,200
we never spray them, we never do anything to them. And yeah, we get some wormy apples.

00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:31,680
We don't even, you know, there's a whole bunch of different tricks that you can do by putting

00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:36,720
the apple cider vinegar and pops out on your tree and hang them, hang them from your tree and things

00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:44,480
like that. We don't even do that. So, we get tons and tons of apples. We can, tons of apples, we

00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:51,120
made, we had so many apples, we juiced so much apple juice. We had gallons and gallons of gallons

00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:57,680
of apple juice that we put in the freezer. Freeze is really, really well. We have a dehydrator,

00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:05,440
we dehydrated a bunch of apple slices. And we have a freeze dryer. We freeze dry tons of apples.

00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:11,520
So much that we, you're just like, what are we going to do? We used every apple that we possibly could.

00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:18,240
So, I think it's great to have apple trees and fruit trees. I think it's fantastic. We have giant

00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:25,520
beds of strawberries. We have huge mungus, raspberry patch. And I make tons of jam with that. And

00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:33,360
we freeze dry a ton of our berries. They're great for the kids, great kids to eat. So, but it's how

00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:40,640
you grow them, what you're, what you're spraying them. Even with apple trees, they're not spraying

00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:46,960
round up. They'd be spraying something for, the only thing that we'd spray the trees for is to keep

00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:56,160
the worms off of the fruiting bodies so that, you know, that's not an issue, but they wouldn't be

00:03:56,160 --> 00:04:02,160
keeping fruit on the tree anyhow. They'd be picking the fruit because it wouldn't travel well

00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:05,680
and it wouldn't sell well. So, I don't think you have to worry about that.

